<rml>
<head>
	<meta name="folio-size" content="320x320"/>
	<link type="text/template" href="/folio/lib/lib.rml"/>
	<style>
		/*
		 * A stamina wheel: a thick ring beside the character that appears when stamina is spent, empties
		 * clockwise from twelve with what was just spent trailing in red, turns red when run dry and
		 * refills red until it recovers, and fades a moment after it is full. More stamina rings the
		 * first, larger and thinner, and a ring can be part of a circle: only what is owned has a track.
		 * Temporary stamina is yellow.
		 *
		 * The "stamina" model this expects:
		 *
		 *   bShown    bool    up: stamina short, or full for under a second
		 *   Position  string  transform placing it, "translate(Xdp, Ydp)". Optionally followed by
		 *                     "scaleX(S)" to angle it, S the cosine of the angle (3D transforms do
		 *                     not reach the Unreal renderer), and "rotate(Ndeg)" to spin where it
		 *                     fills from
		 *   Wheels    array   one row per ring, innermost first:
		 *     Size        float  outer diameter in dp
		 *     Hole        float  the cut-out, as a percentage of the radius: smaller is thicker
		 *     Length      float  degrees of the ring that exist, 0 to 360: a part ring stops here
		 *     Fill        float  degrees filled, 0 to Length
		 *     Trail       float  degrees the red end reaches, Fill to Length: stamina a moment ago
		 *     bSpent      bool   run dry: the whole fill is red until it recovers
		 *     bTemporary  bool   bonus stamina, yellow, which does not come back once spent
		 *
		 * Everything that changes with stamina is a number; the colours and shapes are built here, in
		 * the expressions below. The game decides when it shows, how fast the trail catches up and what
		 * counts as recovered. docs/tutorials/stamina_wheel.md fills the model.
		 *
		 * Each ring is one disc painted by a conic gradient and hollowed by a radial mask-image, so both
		 * edges are smooth circles at any size. The mask is a render layer: one per ring, and only
		 * while the wheel is shown. It masks decorators; a plain background-color is not masked.
		 */
		body {
			position: relative;
			width: 100%;
			height: 100%;
			background-color: transparent;
		}

		/* A zero-size point the rings centre on. */
		.stamina {
			position: absolute;
			left: 50%;
			top: 50%;
			width: 0;
			height: 0;
			opacity: 0;
			transition: opacity 0.3s cubic-out;
		}
		.stamina.shown { opacity: 1; }

		.ring { position: absolute; }
	</style>
</head>

<body data-model="stamina">
	<div class="stamina" data-class-shown="bShown" data-style-transform="Position">
		<div class="ring" data-for="w : Wheels"
			data-style-width="w.Size + 'dp'"
			data-style-height="w.Size + 'dp'"
			data-style-left="(w.Size / -2) + 'dp'"
			data-style-top="(w.Size / -2) + 'dp'"
			data-style-decorator="'conic-gradient(from 0deg at 50% 50%, '
				+ (w.bSpent ? '#e0424a' : (w.bTemporary ? '#f2d24b' : '#7ed957')) + ' 0deg, '
				+ (w.bSpent ? '#e0424a' : (w.bTemporary ? '#f2d24b' : '#7ed957')) + ' ' + w.Fill + 'deg, '
				+ '#e0424a ' + w.Fill + 'deg, #e0424a ' + w.Trail + 'deg, '
				+ '#0b0b0fa0 ' + w.Trail + 'deg, #0b0b0fa0 ' + w.Length + 'deg, #00000000 ' + w.Length + 'deg, #00000000 360deg)'"
			data-style-mask-image="'radial-gradient(circle farthest-side at 50% 50%, #ffffff00 ' + w.Hole + '%, #ffffffff ' + (w.Hole + 3) + '%, #ffffffff 97%, #ffffff00 100%)'"></div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
